      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you were using Input Emulator, you can instead just use the SteamVR input binding to remap the inputs with less hassle.\n\nThat said, something as frequently used as jump on thumbstick click is an all-round awful idea, regardless of controller.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-26T21:02:23.873Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've found that the Oculus Joystick's are very flimsy when it comes to jumping a lot in game. My last pair of controllers broke due to having the jump button mapped on the right controller to the joystick press. It would be best to have some sort of option in the client to remap the jump button so I don't have to use external mapping solutions like OpenVR Input Emulator as those are too complicated and come with too much profile management. As an avid Oculus user, we really need this.",
